CAVEAT:  One router, two VRFs, two directly attached segments. No inter-VRF route
         leaking, no VRF-aware routing protocol and no second-router VRF peering were
         exercised -- the first because this case tests isolation, the others because
         the bench cannot reach them (see the scope note above). The `ip pim vrf
         <name> rp-address` RPs are both local to the DUT, so no inter-router Register
         path exists in this case; that path is measured in T43863 instead.

