  Method, and the one thing this case had to do differently: under VRF isolation
  NOTHING from eth3 may reach eth4 -- including the routed-ICMP instrument control the
  rest of this group used -- so "a flow that must arrive on the far NIC" is unavailable
  by construction. An ICMP aimed at the DUT's own red SVI was tried and produced no
  reply, because the DUT would have to ARP for the crafted sender 10.38.22.40 and
  nothing answers that ARP. The liveness proof actually used is better suited to the
  case: THE DUT'S OWN PIM HELLOS. With PIM enabled per VRF, the red SVI sends hellos on
  eth3's wire and the BLUE SVI sends them on eth4's wire, so an isolation leg that
  captures `IP p103 10.38.22.66 -> 224.0.0.13` on eth4 while counting zero subject
  frames has proved its own capture alive from traffic the DUT generated. Every
  isolation leg below carries that proof. The second control is the A/B itself: the
  identical leg run again with vlan48's VRF membership as the only change.

