  => STEP 1 PASS: that three-line read-back is itself a result. Multicast routing on
     this build is genuinely PER-VRF and independent of the global table --
     `ip multicast-routing vrf <name>` is not a modifier on a global switch, and the
     global switch remained `no ip multicast-routing` for the whole of this case while
     both VRFs forwarded. (The `show ip pim vrf red` read above is taken after the STEP
     3 move, with both interfaces in red; in the isolation state each VRF holds one of
     them.)

