  => STEP 2 PASS: 0 of 10 MULTICAST and 0 of 10 UNICAST crossed the VRF boundary, on a
     capture proved live by the DUT's own blue-SVI hello arriving in the same leg. The
     zero is therefore a measurement and not a dead instrument -- which matters more
     here than anywhere else in this group, because an isolation case is a case whose
     result IS a zero. The membership exists and is held in blue; the traffic exists and
     is in red; nothing joins them.

STEP 3 -- the A/B: move ONE interface into the other VRF and change nothing else   PASS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  A direct VRF-to-VRF move is refused, which was reconfirmed verbatim:

awplus(config-if)#ip vrf forwarding red          (while vlan48 was in blue)
% vlan48: VRF is already associated

  So the move went via the global domain:

awplus(config-if)#no ip vrf forwarding blue
% All IP addresses configured on interface vlan48 have been removed
awplus(config-if)#ip vrf forwarding red
awplus(config-if)#ip address 10.38.22.66/27
awplus(config-if)#ip pim sparse-mode
awplus(config-if)#ip igmp
awplus#show ip interface brief
[VRF: red]   vlan10 10.38.22.34/27   vlan48 10.38.22.66/27
[VRF: blue]  (no interfaces)

  Re-joined -- the interface changed VRF, so the membership has to be re-sent -- and the
  identical leg was run again:

cap v3-same-vrf-eth4.pcap: 20 frame(s)
  x10 UDP  10.38.22.40 -> 239.30.30.30 :5001 [ours] [eth e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43 -> 01:00:5e:1e:1e:1e]
  x10 ICMP t8/c0 10.38.22.40 -> 10.38.22.65 [ours] [eth e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43 -> 00:0d:b9:55:77:0f]

  => STEP 3 PASS: 10 of 10 for the joined group and 10 of 10 for the unicast control,
     against 0 of 10 and 0 of 10 for the identical leg in STEP 2, with vlan48's VRF
     MEMBERSHIP as the only variable in the whole bench -- same cabling, same addresses,
     same group, same source, same ports. A never-joined control group 239.31.31.31
     carried in the same leg stayed at 0 of 10, so what crossed is what was asked for
     and not everything. That pair of legs is the entire claim of VRF-Lite, measured on
     the wire for the multicast path.

